# The kit's Verus files, one a line: the files `make verus-headers`
# (headers.sh) holds a port's copies of, each to the template of the same
# name in the package's templates/ (/usr/share/proved-port/templates/).
# Each template holds its header, its leading `#` comment, ending before
# a `# kit:` line where it has one, but .chainguard/review-prompt.md,
# which holds its vendored-kit rule (the `- The vendored kit` item). The
# kit's other templates (conformance, consumers, fuzz, test, lint, the
# environments, develop.yaml, deps.yaml) are starting points the port
# reshapes, and are not held.
